{
 "title": "The Rough HAR model - replication spec",
 "hypothesis": "Discrete-time RAR/RHAR with negative MA(1) approximates rough fGn (c1(H) approx linear in H) and captures roughness while HAR captures persistence; out-of-sample it outperforms HAR and matches fBm/fOU at short horizons.",
 "data_sources": [
  "TAQ intraday for ETFs realized variance at 5 minutes M=78",
  "VOLARE database http://volare.unime.it for 40 stocks Jan2 2015 - Jan30 2026",
  "Simulated fBm/fOU paths fine grid 10 sub-steps per day"
 ],
 "sample": "Primary: 10 ETFs (SPY, XLB, XLE, XLF, XLI, XLK, XLP, XLV, XLU, XLY) daily realized variance and realized quarticity from TAQ 5-minute intraday returns. Stocks robustness: 40 individual stocks from VOLARE database. DGP simulation: fBm and fOU sampled at Delta=1/250, kappa in {2,5}, H in {0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4}, n in {500,4000}, 500 replications per cell.",
 "period_start": "January 4, 2010",
 "period_end": "December 31, 2024",
 "method": [
  "1. Intraday: 5-minute returns r_{t,i} over 6.5-hour day, M=78. RV_t=sum r^2, RQ_t=M/3 sum r^4, BPV_t=mu1^{-2} sum |r_{t,i}||r_{t,i+1}| mu1=sqrt(2/pi), J_t=max[RV_t-BPV_t,0], RS_t^+=sum r^2 I(r>0), RS_t^-=sum r^2 I(r<0). y_j=log RV_j.",
  "2. Continuous-time models: fBm y_t=sigma B^H_t Whittle estimator of Fukasawa-Takabatake 2019, fOU dy=kappa(mu-y)dt+sigma dB^H ML of Wang-Xiao-Yu-Zhang 2025 with Delta=1/250 kappa per year. Discrete-time: AR y_j=omega+rho y_{j-1}+epsilon_j, RAR epsilon_j=varepsilon_j+theta varepsilon_{j-1}, HAR y_j=omega+rho1 y_{j-1}+rho2 y_{j-1|j-5}+rho3 y_{j-1|j-22}+epsilon_j where y_{j-i|j-l}=1/(l-i+1) sum y_{j-p}, RHAR same with MA(1), HARQ RV_t=beta0+(beta1+beta1Q RQ_{t-1}^{1/2})RV_{t-1}+beta2 RV_{t-1|t-5}+beta3 RV_{t-1|t-22}+u_t, HARJ RV_t=beta0+beta1 RV_{t-1}+beta2 RV_{t-1|t-5}+beta3 RV_{t-1|t-22}+beta_j J_{t-1}+u_t, HARS RV_{t+h}=beta0+beta1^+ RS_t^+ +beta1^- RS_t^- +beta2 RV_{t|t-4}+beta3 RV_{t|t-21}+eps. AR/HAR OLS, RAR/RHAR exact ML via Kalman filter, SEs: fBm/fOU analytic asymptotic, AR/HAR OLS, RAR OPG, RHAR Hessian.",
  "3. Wold approximation: fGn spectral density f(lambda)=2C_H(1-cos lambda)(2pi)^{-1-2H}[zeta(1+2H,1-lambda/2pi)+zeta(1+2H,lambda/2pi)] C_H=sigma^2(2pi)^{-1}Gamma(2H+1)sin(pi H). Compute cepstral a_k=1/(2pi)int log f e^{-ik lambda}d lambda on midpoint grid via FFT, recursion c_{k+1}=sum_{j=0}^k (1-j/(k+1)) a_{k+1-j}c_j c0=1, approximate infinite sum by first 100 terms. c1(H) monotonic approx linear -1 to 0.",
  "4. Simulation DGP: fOU exact discretization y_{iDelta}=exp(-kappa Delta) y_{(i-1)Delta}+(1-exp(-kappa Delta))mu+eta eta=sigma int e^{-kappa(iDelta-s)} dB^H_s, approximated on fine grid 10 sub-steps per day midpoint integration, burn-in 500 days discarded. H={0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4} kappa={2,5} n={500,4000} 500 replications, estimate RAR/RHAR ML Kalman, invert c1(.) to H_imp restricted to H in (0,0.5). At most 6/500 per cell non-converged excluded. Pile-up at invertibility boundary capped just inside.",
  "5. Forecasting: rolling window 500 trading days (~2 years) rolled 1 day, re-estimate each step, h-ahead forecasts for 1-day, 1-week (5 days), 1-month (22 days). Log models convert via log-normal correction RVhat=exp(yhat+s_hat_h^2/2). Insanity filter: forecast outside [min RV in window, max RV in window] replaced by mean in window. Losses MSE=(RVhat-RV)^2 QLIKE=RV/RVhat -log(RV/RVhat)-1. Ratio to HAR benchmark.",
  "6. Inference: MCS model confidence set Hansen-Lunde-Nason 2011 T_{max,M_s}=max studentized average loss differential, block bootstrap block length 20 5000 replications. Null H0,M_s: E(d_{ij,t})=0 for all i,j in M_s, alternative !=0. Stars: *** 75% set p>0.25, ** 90% set p>0.10, * 95% set p>0.05. p-values reported per ETF per horizon per loss for 10 models.",
  "7. Measurement error check: y_j=x_j+w_j x_j=omega+phi x_{j-1}+v_j+theta v_{j-1} with sigma_w^2=1/39 fixed (=2/m m=78) from Fukasawa et al 2022 asymptotic w~N(0,2/m) independent. Estimate by ML Kalman, test theta=0.",
  "8. Nulls/benchmarks: H=0.5 Brownian null, H<0.5 rough, d=H-0.5 ARFIMA link, HAR benchmark ratio=1.0000."
 ],
